Backport to esp-nimble 139cada (ESP-IDF v6.1) of the stale ack drain in
ble_hs_hci_cmd_tx() from espressif/esp-nimble
  d7061976e9a10b18ddd41ecdf118f039b8d34477 (free a stale ack before sending)
  79316193f942060e9c79200ddd032157453b041d (always drain the semaphore)
Both are on nimble-1.10.0-idf and in ESP-IDF master, not in release/v6.1.

A command that times out after BLE_HCI_CMD_TIMEOUT_MS schedules a host reset.
When its ack arrives late, ble_hs_hci_rx_ack() stores it and releases the
semaphore, then the timed out call frees the ack and leaves the semaphore at 1.
The reset's HCI_Reset takes that stale count at once and
ble_hs_hci_process_ack() reads the NULL ack (LoadProhibited, CoreS3 bench
2026-10-18). Draining first makes the reset wait for its own ack.

--- a/nimble/host/src/ble_hs_hci.c
+++ b/nimble/host/src/ble_hs_hci.c
@@ -592,6 +592,17 @@ ble_hs_hci_cmd_tx(uint16_t opcode, const void *cmd, uint8_t cmd_len,

     BLE_HS_DBG_ASSERT(l_ble_hs_hci_ack == NULL);
     ble_hs_hci_lock();
+    if (l_ble_hs_hci_ack != NULL) {
+#if MYNEWT_VAL(MP_RUNTIME_ALLOC)
+        ble_transport_free(BLE_HCI_EVT, (uint8_t *)l_ble_hs_hci_ack);
+#else
+        ble_transport_free((uint8_t *)l_ble_hs_hci_ack);
+#endif
+        l_ble_hs_hci_ack = NULL;
+    }
+    /* A late ack of a timed out command left the count at 1. */
+    ble_npl_sem_pend(&ble_hs_hci_sem, 0);
+    BLE_HS_DBG_ASSERT(l_ble_hs_hci_ack == NULL);

     rc = ble_hs_hci_cmd_send_buf(opcode, cmd, cmd_len);
     if (rc != 0) {
